.TH USB-AUTOMOUNT 8 "2026-08-27" "usb-automount 2.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
usb-automount \- automatic USB storage device mounting for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-automount.sh
.I device
.I action
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-automount
automatically mounts and unmounts USB and SD-card filesystem partitions on Linux
systems. It is designed for headless servers, Raspberry Pi, and minimal desktop
environments where no graphical file manager handles removable storage.
.PP
Devices are mounted using their filesystem label when available, for example
.IR /media/MY_USB_DRIVE ,
falling back to a device name such as
.IR /media/usb-sdb1 .
.PP
Executable post-mount and post-unmount hooks can trigger automated actions such
as backups or synchronization.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in
.IR /etc/usb-automount/usb-automount.conf .
.TP
.B MOUNT_DIR
Base directory for mount points. Default:
.IR /media .
.TP
.B USE_LABEL
Use filesystem labels for mount point names. Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B MIN_PARTITION_SIZE
Minimum partition size in bytes to mount. Default:
.IR 104857600
(100 MiB).
.TP
.B EXCLUDED_DEVICES
Comma-separated list of device names to never mount.
.TP
.B LOG_FILE
Log file path. Default:
.IR /var/log/usb-automount.log .
.TP
.B NOTIFY
Desktop notification mode:
.IR auto ,
.IR always ,
or
.IR never .
.TP
.B HOOKS_DIR
Directory containing executable hook scripts. Default:
.IR /etc/usb-automount/hooks.d .
.SH HOOKS
Executable scripts in the hooks directory run after successful mount and
unmount operations. They receive these environment variables:
.TP
.B USB_DEVICE
Device name, for example sdb1.
.TP
.B USB_MOUNTPOINT
Mount point path.
.TP
.B USB_FSTYPE
Filesystem type.
.TP
.B USB_LABEL
Filesystem label, which may be empty.
.TP
.B USB_UUID
Filesystem UUID, which may be empty.
.TP
.B USB_ACTION
Either
.B post-mount
or
.BR post-unmount .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/usb-automount.sh
Main script.
.TP
.I /etc/usb-automount/usb-automount.conf
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/usb-automount/hooks.d/
Hook scripts directory.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-usb-automount.rules
udev rules.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/usb-automount@.service
systemd template service.
.TP
.I /var/log/usb-automount.log
Log file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install usb-automount:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo ./install.sh
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create a backup hook:
.PP
.nf
.RS
#!/bin/bash
if [ "$USB_ACTION" = "post-mount" ] && [ "$USB_UUID" = "1234-ABCD" ]; then
    rsync -av /home/user/docs/ "$USB_MOUNTPOINT/backup/"
fi
.RE
.fi
